comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-07T21:59:42.443Z",codex-sol,"The first full release run failed eight assertions across extension routes, spawn fallback and project routes because extensionless CommonJS fixture scripts inherited an ambient ESM package scope. Focused extension-route validation passes 9/9 using an isolated scratch root with an explicit CommonJS package scope. Both full release runners use that isolation without changing fixtures or weakening assertions."
  "2026-10-07T22:02:46.842Z",codex-sol,"A full run with the scratch root nested inside the checkout resolves the ESM failures but exposes two omit-dev fixture failures: Node resolves pm-ops from the ancestor node_modules. Final gate isolation uses a dedicated external scratch root with explicit CommonJS scope and its own Git repository. The scratch Git repository also contains automatic merge-driver registration from tracker initialization. Generated package attributes from the nested attempt were restored; no upstream issue was filed."
  "2026-10-07T22:09:13.654Z",codex-sol,"External scratch-root validation passes all seven prepare-merge-driver tests, including omit-dev and malformed lookup cases. The final full coverage run passes 484/484 with the same isolation and no fixture edits. PM SDK catalog acceptance found no new defect; CLI tracker initialization's automatic ancestor Git attribute registration must be contained by scratch Git isolation."
  "2026-10-07T22:17:01.464Z",codex-sol,Both full release gates now pass 484/484 using external scratch-root CommonJS and Git isolation. Fixture hardening remains open and unclaimed as follow-up work; no assertions were weakened or fixtures changed in this catalog PR.
  "2026-10-21T19:37:58.097Z",codex-agent,"Duplicate of pm-web-sspv. Reverified main ca7e188bc91e (unchanged since audit): Canonical id: pm-web-sspv for the identical three-suite ambient ESM fixture failure. Its extra omit-dev ancestor-leak caution should remain a fixture-isolation acceptance note, not a third duplicate issue. Retained evidence: test/extensions-routes.test.ts, test/pm-runner.test.ts, test/projects-routes.test.ts."
